{:edb/db-before-t 1458 :edb/db-after-t 1459 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534771 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:26:23.676Z" 13194139534771 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309082 13194139534771 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309096 13194139534771 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309089 13194139534771 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309103 13194139534771 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309110 13194139534771 true] [17592186309082 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309083 13194139534771 true] [17592186309082 1089 "q-21504" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309082 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534771 true] [17592186309082 1100 "For the function $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+36x-48,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=3$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(3)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=3$" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309082 1113 #uuid "272ae442-0eb1-5b16-aba6-999ab95c4bf6" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309082 1145 "We need to identify whether $x=3$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+36x-48,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-12x+36,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12x+36 & =0 \\\\ -12(x-3) & =0 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have a critical point at $x=3.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-12,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=3$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(3)=-12<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=3,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=3$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(3)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=3\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534771 true]