e true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1$" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309089 1113 #uuid "11a248cf-66d8-5ef2-be89-74a7b6dbe4ae" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309089 1145 "We're given that $x=-1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=4{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}-20x+30,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=20({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-x-1).\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=20(4{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =20(4(-1)^{3}+3(-1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =20(-4+3-1) \\\\  & =-40<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309091 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309092 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309093 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309094 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309095 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1041 "selection" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309091 13194139534771 true] [17592186309090 1110 #uuid "4ec32751-2902-5efd-b882-aad408b5f4c3" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309091 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309091 1111 #uuid "44aa782b-d055-5d93-a386-a8b49b828205" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309092 1034 "I only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309092 1111 #uuid "ee4a7a56-3a5c-58a5-be69-0682d73bde4a" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309093 1034 "III only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309093 1111 #uuid "c6cff171-ef3f-5d60-a9f7-a8307991cad6" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309094 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309094 1111 #uuid "be13dfee-3409-5074-a64d-603766a3f42c" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309095 1034 "II only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309095 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309095 1111 #uuid "86953212-600f-5b8d-ad71-5809e02af13e" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309096 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309097 13194139534771 true] [17592186309096 1089 "q-22080" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309096 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534771 true] [17592186309096 1100 "For the function $f(x)={x}^{5}-5{x}^{3}+15,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=\\sqrt{3}$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(\\sqrt{3})<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309096 1113 #uuid "686a27c2-b67a-56d7-83b5-6def2ee11b09" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309096 1145 "We need to identify whether $x=\\sqrt{3}$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)={x}^{5}-5{x}^{3}+15,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{4}-15{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{4}-15{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-3) & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}(x+\\sqrt{3})(x-\\sqrt{3}) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{3},0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3},0.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=20{x}^{3}-30x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\sqrt{3})=20(\\sqrt{3})^{3}-30\\sqrt{3}=30\\sqrt{3}>0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=\\sqrt{3},$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=\\sqrt{3}$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\sqrt{3})<0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=\\sqrt{3}\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309098 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309099 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309100 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309101 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309102 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1041 "selection" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309099 13194139534771 true] [17592186309097 1110 #uuid "bca72a99-5383-5f75-9603-5becf96eaaa9" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309098 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309098 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309098 1111 #uuid "b6c1e0e1-d791-5714-ba86-1da24f9494e2" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309099 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309099 1111 #uuid "7fa13942-2c37-5749-a0d2-3eafc793a16b" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309100 1034 "I only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309100 1111 #uuid "bc82bcdc-1f77-5f0d-89ef-3d71fc054705" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309101 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309101 1111 #uuid "82eb78a7-6574-57cd-86e8-e94dd5b4f41a" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309102 1034 "II only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309102 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309102 1111 #uuid "29b53951-f44b-5069-8357-9d7af07393ec" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309103 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309104 13194139534771 true] [17592186309103 1089 "q-22187" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309103 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534771 true] [17592186309103 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+3x+3.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{2})=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\frac{1}{2}$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=\\frac{1}{2}$" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309103 1113 #uuid "1df74f84-f65d-533a-a7f9-fc6a2bfb54bc" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309103 1145 "We're given that $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+3x+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{2}-12x+3=3(2x-1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=24x-12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =24(\\frac{1}{2})-12=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=0,1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =3(2\\cdot 0-1)^{2}=3>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =3(2\\cdot 1-1)^{2}=3>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=\\frac{1}{2}$, we conclude that $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309105 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309106 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309107 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309108 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309109 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1041 "selection" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309106 13194139534771 true] [17592186309104 1110 #uuid "14e030bd-d590-53f3-a5f0-5c3420fa66c0" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309105 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309105 1111 #uuid "86648d9c-87f0-512b-8666-615f45ab673d" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309106 1034 "I only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309106 1111 #uuid "26248452-dfee-5abe-8134-9c0e3337a763" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309107 1034 "III only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309107 1111 #uuid "107b2a34-5585-523b-8d78-8961db0c3712" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309108 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309108 1111 #uuid "738917c7-e8af-57b0-9dc3-5482f09d0d8b" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309109 1034 "II only" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534771 true] [17592186309109 1111 #uuid "3cc5787d-23a5-52a2-8acb-03de18913649" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309110 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309111 13194139534771 true] [17592186309110 1089 "q-22561" 13194139534771 true] [17592186309110 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534771 true] [17592186309110 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2}).$ Given that ${f}^{′}(0)=0,$ which of the fo